  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 246 PM EDT Thu Apr 16 2026\n\nWeekend frontal boundary with precip chances increasing.\n\nBeginning Sat...High pressure continuing across the area begins to \nbreak down as next frontal boundary nears the state. SW flow ahead \nof the front will help to keep temps elevated with highs across \nnorth and central GA in the upper 80s to middle 90s. The frontal \nboundary pushes through the MS river valley and into NW GA around \n00z-03z Sun. As the front pushes into the state it weakens and \nbegins to dry out. Most locations across North and wester central GA \nwill see some precip Sat night but it will be less and less the \nfurther it moves south and east into the area. This front will be \npushing into a very dry airmass with precip chances (30% or higher) \nonly making it as far south as the SW ATL suburbs. This boundary has \nvery little instability/buoyancy associated with it, Thus, severe \nweather is not expected. \n\nUnfortunately, with this front drying as it moves into the area, \nprecip amounts will do the same.  rainfall is likely to remain \naround 0.25 inches or less with some isolated locations across NW GA \nseeing 0.75\" or less. While any rainfall at all is much welcomed, no \ndrought improvements will come from such small totals. The cold \nfront passage will be noticeable on Sunday, with high temperatures \npotentially some 15-20 degrees cooler than they were on Saturday. \nMonday morning lows could be as chilly as the upper 30s to lower 40s \nacross parts of the area. Widespread lows in the 40s are currently \nforecast for early Tuesday morning. \n\nFire weather conditions will continue into next week as another dry \nand cooler airmass moves into the state behind the frontal boundary. \nThe post-front environment on Monday and Tuesday looks to bring a \nvery dry airmass with relative humidity currently progged to be in \nthe teens-to-20 percent range -- plenty dry enough for continued \nissuances of fire weather products.",
